Description: Erase network-layer identifiers on Linux
 Proteus rotates and scrubs the identifiers your laptop broadcasts when
 joining a network: MAC address, DHCP options 12/60/61/81, IPv6 stable
 privacy + DUID, hostname, Bluetooth alias, mDNS announcements, and
 TCP/ICMP stack fingerprint. CLI-first; designed to be GUI-wrappable.
